      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "6600dd84-6e27-5db7-808d-018410e86c74",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jomar Brun\n- Events: World War II, Operation Freshman, Operation Gunnerside, Norwegian heavy water sabotage\n- Places: London, Vemork\n- Concepts: heavy water, deuterium oxide, German nuclear weapon project\n\nFacts:\n- During World War II, Jomar Brun was called to London and contributed to the planning phase of Operation Freshman and Operation Gunnerside.\n- Operation Freshman and Operation Gunnerside were part of the heavy water sabotage at Vemork.\n- The Norwegian heavy water sabotage was a series of operations carried out by Norwegian saboteurs during World War II.\n- The Norwegian heavy water sabotage aimed to prevent the German nuclear weapon project from acquiring heavy water, or deuterium oxide, that could have been used to produce nuclear weapons.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
